        ":question/id": "f46348e6-eb61-5dc8-a24d-6bb638a9f7eb",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "$\\int \\frac{3}{x \\log_{5}\\left(x\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\log_{5}\\left(x\\right).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\,\\Longrightarrow\\,\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{x \\log_{5}\\left(x\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\log_{5}\\left(x\\right)}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3 \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3 \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}\\cdot \\ln\\left|u\\right|+C \\\\  & =3 \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)} \\ln\\left|\\log_{5}\\left(x\\right)\\right|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
